  "why": "The statement asks only about bounding Δₖ(x) and names no exponent value, so the most anything could deliver is a bound on Δₖ for some k. I read 'bounding' as covering Ω-type lower bounds as well as upper bounds. On that reading the log-power sharpenings by Sourmelidis, Mahatab and Lamzouri move a quantity on the problem itself (the size of Δ over the integers) and count as bound. The number-field Ω papers change the setting, so they are variant. Tudzi and Palojärvi–Tudzi give explicit bounds at exponents worse than the known asymptotic record, which is an effective form of the problem rather than a move on αₖ, so they are variant. Sums of Δₖ(n), the smoothed sum and joint sign changes concern neighbouring objects and are also variant. Elaissaoui states no bound, so it is none. Runbo Li claims an upper-exponent improvement but is known only from snippets. Because it is a modest numerical claim and not a landmark one, the F10 threshold for not_credible is not met, so I kept it as doubtful. Bourgain–Watt is knocked down by its own withdrawal. Journal publication counts as digested; preprints count as unreviewed. No event credits an AI system.",
